## Why This Is Asked

This question probes designing a latency-sensitive, privacy-respecting, explainable inference service with multi-tenant isolation in AWS, plus lifecycle and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink, VPC, Private Data Lake, per-tenant isolation
- SageMaker endpoints, Feature Store, Model Registry
- Real-time explainability paths (Clarify/SHAP) with low latency
- Canary rollout, drift detection, monitoring and cost

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: route to appropriate prod/canary endpoint
function route(tenantId){
  const inCanary = ['tenantA','tenantB'];
  const ep = inCanary.includes(tenantId) ? 'fraud-prod-canary' : 'fraud-prod';
  return ep;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce strict per-tenant data access controls across services?
- How would you validate explainability fidelity at high throughput?
- How would you handle retraining triggers when drift is detected per tenant?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to integrate explainability, bias auditing, drift monitoring, and controlled deployment in a multi-tenant, VPC-isolated AWS environment.

## Key Concepts

- SageMaker Clarify for bias and explainability
- Model Monitor drift detection
- PrivateLink and private feature store integration
- Canary rollout with per-tenant isolation
- Auditable logging to S3

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing snippet for multi-tenant endpoint
function routeTenant(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const endpoint = `rt-endpoint-${tenant}`;
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, req.body);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce data leakage prevention across tenants?
- How would you scale explainability reporting for thousands of tenants?
